  "interfaces": {
    "critical_scope": "The complete actual critical configuration, opposite natural tails and disjoint head supports are inherited with their full predecessor proofs and explicit smaller-degree induction. No new rank induction is used in this packet.",
    "paired_middle": "The complete early-colour and transitive-B results give the four boundary colours. A hypothetical unique middle cut has no shared labels by the actual prefix-orbit lemma and its full reversal; the accepted later-unshared theorem excludes its index.",
    "odd_prefix": "The natural prefix C has rank r-3 and odd degree 2(r-3)+1. Every local maximal omission is intransitive by adjoining the actual right head. The natural left tail is proved by the actual intersection, and eligibility is transferred only in the valid ambient-to-subgroup direction.",
    "fixed_point_transfer": "The right exit vertex is moved by the final prefix mark and is excluded from every local nonterminal fixed set. All three later marks are supported on the right head and fix all other points of the prefix domain.",
    "reversed_prefix_count": "The actual intersection J=R intersect C removes exactly five right-head points from the support while retaining the nontrivial orbit count. The degree-two reduced head orbit is checked through the literal crossing. Ambient interval counting gives q<=2 and at most 2s+2 full fixed points.",
    "exterior_pair_forest": "For q=2 the exact support equality has size 2d+1. If left delta is nontrivial on the exterior orbit, use actual tau=rho3 as the pair switch in every relevant ambient omission. Complementary eligible colours are confined to the one reduced head orbit; the full selected-localization theorem applies to arbitrary subsets of its interval.",
    "separator_proof_use": "The final proof explicitly replays the delta-fixed subsets supplied in every complete witness proof, rather than infer them from the numerical separator statement. The transitive-witness exception is handled by the distinct two-point copy and parity.",
    "literal_pair": "Once delta is literally one transposition on the full domain, the exterior-pair obstruction is applied inside the odd prefix C, whose actual hypotheses and paired colours were verified. It is not applied to the unpaired right-head colours of the full group."
  },
  "new_statements": [
    "Every central colour 3 through r-4 is ambient paired under opposite actual heads.",
    "The odd-prefix separator has its fixed points preserved by the actual opposite head attachment.",
    "The later support has at most two nontrivial orbits, the left odd exterior involution fixes that support pointwise, and its full fixed set has at most 2s+2 points.",
    "The actual opposite six-point heads are impossible throughout the critical range n=2r>=18."
  ],
  "new_rank_induction_or_computation": false,
  "pending_packets_used_as_premises": false,
  "contributions": "The retained pure-prefix parity-fibre idea and selected-localization middle move were contributed by the root collaborator and already distinctly reviewed. The single-separator transfer, opposite-prefix support count and final fixed-set parity argument are this author continuation."
}
